      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I was considering making a &quot;Villain Analogues&quot; thread to match the Hero one in Rules And Gameplay, but decided that my analyses of the villains aren&#39;t nearly as snappy as the Hero ones, so people would either be bored by explanations of how Fright Train is clearly The Juggernaut, or confused by why I equate The Chairman with Baron Strucker.</p><p>Or maybe just confused about who Baron Strucker even is.</p><p>But I had to post just one of these analyses, the one nearest and dearest to my heart, which I suspect not everyone sees the way I do.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.15;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a8b455d9-8f20-6d23-cc67-44f6329434e5\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px; font-family: Arial; white-space: pre-wrap;\">La Capitan, you see, is an analogue to my favorite super-villain of all time: Carmen Sandiego.</span></span></p><p><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a8b455d9-8f20-6d23-cc67-44f6329434e5\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px; font-family: Arial; white-space: pre-wrap;\">No, think about it: she&rsquo;s a badass hispanic thief, you spend a goodly portion of the game chasing after her rather than fighting her directly, and she has a collection of colorful named henchmen with their own skills and backgrounds. &nbsp;And La Paradoja Magnifica manages to cover all of her vehicle needs by being both a flying machine </span><span style=\"font-size: 15px; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; white-space: pre-wrap;\">and</span><span style=\"font-size: 15px; font-family: Arial; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> a time machine! &nbsp;Throw in elbow-length brown hair combined with a signature coat and broad-brimmed hat, and it becomes a lock.</span></span></p><p><span><span style=\"font-size: 15px; font-family: Arial; white-space: pre-wrap;\">(Good luck getting Rockapella out of your heard for the rest of today, by the way.)</span></span></p>",
