    {
      "id": 94651,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-05T17:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Edwin\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Edwin:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span>I figure La Capitan is analogous to Kang the Conqueror, only Latina and with a different attitude (more sprightly than domineering). <span></span></span></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><span>People keep saying this, but I don't see it.</span></p>\n<p><span>Sure, they are both villains who use time travel and oppose a team of four fantastic family members. &nbsp;But do they have literally&nbsp;<em>anything</em> else in common?</span></p>\n<p><span>Kang:</span></p>\n<ul><li>From the future.</li><li>Is an authoritarian ruler.</li><li>Motivated by personal tragedy.</li><li>Battles using an array of machines and countermeasures, with few if any human servants.</li></ul>\nLa Capitan:\n<ul><li>From the past.</li><li>Is a countercultural rebel.</li><li>Motivated by excitement and greed.</li><li>Battles using a team of colorful allies, with minimal reliance on their advanced technology.</li></ul>\nI... really don't see it. &nbsp;If anything, you could make a case for any given Legion Of Superheroes villain, like Emerald Empress.",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:21:14.389Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
