      "raw": "[quote=\"Edwin\"]\n<span style=\"font-size: 13.333333969116211px;\">I figure La Capitan is analogous to Kang the Conqueror, only Latina and with a different attitude (more sprightly than domineering). <span style=\"font-size: 13.333333969116211px;\">\n[/quote]\n \n\n<span style=\"font-size: 13.333333969116211px;\">People keep saying this, but I don&#39;t see it. \n\n<span style=\"font-size: 13.333333969116211px;\">Sure, they are both villains who use time travel and oppose a team of four fantastic family members. &nbsp;But do they have literally&nbsp;<em>anything</em> else in common? \n\n<span style=\"font-size: 13.333333969116211px;\">Kang: \n<ul><li>From the future.</li><li>Is an authoritarian ruler.</li><li>Motivated by personal tragedy.</li><li>Battles using an array of machines and countermeasures, with few if any human servants.</li></ul>\nLa Capitan:\n<ul><li>From the past.</li><li>Is a countercultural rebel.</li><li>Motivated by excitement and greed.</li><li>Battles using a team of colorful allies, with minimal reliance on their advanced technology.</li></ul>\nI... really don&#39;t see it. &nbsp;If anything, you could make a case for any given Legion Of Superheroes villain, like Emerald Empress.\n",
