      "username": "Edwin",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-05T22:31:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ironic\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/48/2171_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ironic:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>People keep saying this, but I don't see it.Sure, they are both villains who use time travel and oppose a team of four fantastic family members. &nbsp;But do they have literally&nbsp;<em>anything</em> else in common?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not really; I figure that's enough.&nbsp; Cappy is pretty much \"an authoritarian ruler\" over her crew though; I don't see anything about her being a \"countercultural rebel\".&nbsp; And all of her colorful allies are using advanced technology.</p>",
